---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
	<div class="page-shell prose">
		<section aria-labelledby="about-heading">
			<p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
			<h1 id="about-heading">Mapping Kirkbride asylums</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				Asylum Atlas is an in-progress map-based index of former and surviving US sites associated
				with the Kirkbride Plan.
			</p>
			<p>
				Use the map to explore sites by name, location, current status, and available imagery. Each
				record keeps its history, uncertainty, and sources visible.
			</p>
			<h2>Why though?</h2>
			<p>
				I've been fascinated by Kirkbride buildings, both their architectural and historical legacy,
				for several years. While there are many great sources of information online (many of which
				I've read exhaustively and were used as sources for this site), I'd never seen a map of all
				known site locations alongside their essential details and current status. As a software
				engineer and mapping specialist, I felt compelled to change that.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
	.lead {
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}
	.prose .button {
		color: var(--paper);
	}
</style>
